{"chunk_id": "db841c3723da", "text": "This section briefly compresses the rise and fall of the Pandavas before transitioning to the formal beginning of the Mahabharata narrative. After returning to Hastinapura, the Pandavas are given Khandavaprastha to avoid conflict with their cousins. From this base they expand their power, conquering the four directions. Arjuna later spends years in exile, marries Krishna\u2019s sister Subhadra, helps Agni burn the Khandava forest, and receives the divine bow Gandiva. The rescued Asura Maya builds the magnificent palace that later provokes Duryodhana\u2019s jealousy. Through deceitful dice play engineered by Shakuni, the Pandavas are exiled for thirteen years, eventually returning to claim their kingdom, which leads to the great war and their victory. King Janamejaya, hearing this brief outline, asks for the full story, prompting the formal recitation of the vast epic by Vaisampayana.\nPandavas rise to power, Arjuna gains Subhadra and Gandiva, Maya builds their palace, Duryodhana\u2019s envy leads to dice exile; Janamejaya asks for the full story.\nThemes: rise of the Pandavas, divine weapons and alliances, envy and deception, origin of the dice exile, framing of the epic narration", "vector": [0.007561941165477037, -0.029449669644236565, -0.004924905486404896, 0.0006763015990145504, -0.03136509656906128, 0.024355169385671616, -0.008240320719778538, -0.016041690483689308, -0.011120110750198364, -0.018662098795175552, 0.021162793040275574, -0.002633710391819477, 0.014285883866250515, 0.019327176734805107, -0.0002936736564151943, 0.01383362989872694, 0.03607385233044624, -0.0283589418977499, 0.01296902820467949, -0.02682926133275032, -0.002711856970563531, -0.024794122204184532, -0.004319684114307165, 0.014831247739493847, -0.011918204836547375, 0.024927137419581413, 0.0077149090357124805, -0.011884951032698154, 0.017105815932154655, -0.00032942162943072617, -0.020883461460471153, -0.0006048056529834867, 0.008306829258799553, 0.001